title: Fiscal Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: fiscal_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and finance_minister_party = "SPD" and fiscal_policy_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/HilferdingRudolf.jpg
go-to: fiscal_menu

= Fiscal Policy

We run the finance ministry. Taxes, the budget and the debt brake are ours to shape.

@fiscal_menu

Taxes on high incomes and wealth: [+ upper_tax_rates : taxation +]

Taxes on low incomes and consumption: [+ lower_tax_rates : taxation +]

- @raise_rich: Increase taxes on the rich.
- @raise_poor
- @raise_overall: Increase overall taxes.
- @cut_rich
- @cut_poor
- @cut_overall: Cut overall taxes.
- @raise_progressive: Make the tax system more progressive by raising taxes on the rich and cutting them for the poor.
- @regressive
- @tariffs
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@raise_progressive
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 : Taxes on low incomes are too low to cut any further. ?] [? if upper_tax_rates > 5 : Taxes on the rich are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; fdp_relation -= 4; finance_goal_completed += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1

We raise the top rate and cut income tax for low and middle earners. Our base is pleased, while our partners on the centre-right and the better-off are not.

@raise_rich
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; coalition_dissent += 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5; budget += 2; fdp_relation -= 4; unemployment_rate += 0.2; finance_goal_completed += 1; inflation -= 0.2; economic_growth -= 0.2; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; left_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3

[? if upper_tax_rates == 1 : We raise the top rate of income tax. ?][? if upper_tax_rates == 2 : We reform the inheritance tax, so that large company fortunes no longer pass on tax-free. ?][? if upper_tax_rates >= 3 : We bring back the wealth tax, suspended since 1997. ?] Our base is pleased. Business groups warn of capital flight.

@raise_poor
title: Raise VAT.
subtitle: +2 budget. This falls hardest on people with low incomes.
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 2; workers_spd -= 4; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; labor_dissent += 3; left_dissent += 3; inflation += 0.3

We raise VAT. It brings in money quickly, but people with low incomes spend all they earn and so pay the most, as our voters notice.

@cut_overall
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 5*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.4 if unemployment_rate >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.3; economic_growth += 0.3;

A broad tax cut helps the middle class and the better-off most, since they pay the most tax. Our partners on the centre-right are pleased.

@cut_poor
title: Cut taxes for low and middle incomes.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; lower_tax_rates -= 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.2 if unemployment_rate >= 5; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.2; finance_goal_completed += 1; labor_dissent -= 3; left_dissent -= 3;

We raise the basic tax allowance and cut social contributions for low earners.

@cut_rich
title: Cut taxes for high earners and companies.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; upper_tax_rates -= 1; new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 4*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.2 if unemployment_rate >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.2; labor_dissent += 3; left_dissent += 3

We cut corporate tax and abolish the remaining solidarity surcharge. The Union and the FDP approve.

@raise_overall
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; new_middle_spd -= 4; old_middle_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 4; unemployment_rate += 0.4; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 2; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.3; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

Raising taxes hurts our support among everyone who pays them. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition : Our partners prefer this kind of "shared sacrifice" to simply taxing the rich, however. ?] Higher taxes also mean less demand, and perhaps more unemployment.

@regressive
title: Cut taxes on the rich and raise VAT.
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 : Taxes on the rich are too low to cut any further. ?] [? if lower_tax_rates > 5 : Taxes on low incomes are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 6; new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5; cdu_relation += 4; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; labor_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5

This helps the better-off at the expense of low earners. Our partners on the centre-right approve.

@tariffs
title: Deal with the debt brake instead.

The debt brake in the Basic Law limits new federal borrowing to 0.35% of GDP. Since 2025, defence spending and the infrastructure fund are exempt, but everything else is still bound by it. Changing it needs a two-thirds majority.

- @reform_debt_brake
- @fiscal_menu: Change taxes instead.
- @root: Leave the debt brake as it is.
- @easy_discard

@reform_debt_brake
title: Reform the debt brake to allow borrowing for public investment.
subtitle: +3 budget. Needs a two-thirds majority in the Bundestag and the Bundesrat.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_in_government = 0 and cdu_relation < 50 : Without the Union, there is no two-thirds majority. ?]
choose-if: cdu_in_government = 1 or cdu_relation >= 50
view-if: debt_brake_reformed = 0
on-arrival: debt_brake_reformed = 1; budget += 3; fdp_relation -= 10; cdu_relation -= 3; greens_relation += 3; left_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent += 3; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.3
max-visits: 1

After months of negotiations, the debt brake is reformed: borrowing for schools, rail and climate is now allowed within strict limits. The FDP calls it the end of fiscal responsibility, and the Bundesbank is sceptical.
